\section{Implementation}
\label{sec:implementation}

This section provides comprehensive details about the technical implementation of the Solar Energy Monitoring and Control System, including development decisions, component architecture, technology integration, and deployment strategies. The implementation follows industry best practices and modern software engineering principles.

\subsection{Development Decisions and Technical Rationale}
\label{subsec:development-decisions-rationale}

The implementation decisions were made based on careful analysis of requirements, performance considerations, maintainability factors, and long-term evolution needs.

\subsubsection{Technology Stack Selection Rationale}
\label{subsubsec:tech-stack-rationale}

\paragraph{Backend Technology Decisions}

\textbf{Java 21 and Spring Boot 3.3.4 Selection}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Decision Rationale}: 
        \begin{itemize}
            \item \textbf{Modern Language Features}: Record classes and pattern matching for cleaner code
            \item \textbf{Type Safety}: Compile-time error detection reduces runtime issues
            \item \textbf{Ecosystem Maturity}: Extensive libraries and frameworks available
            \item \textbf{Enterprise Features}: Built-in security, monitoring, and configuration management as seen in \texttt{pom.xml}
            \item \textbf{Long-term Support}: Oracle's LTS guarantee for Java 21
        \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Alternatives Evaluated}:
        \begin{itemize}
            \item \textbf{Node.js}: Rejected due to type safety concerns and less robust enterprise features
            \item \textbf{Python (Django/FastAPI)}: Rejected due to performance requirements for real-time processing
            \item \textbf{Go}: Rejected due to limited ecosystem for rapid development
            \item \textbf{C\# (.NET Core)}: Rejected due to team expertise and cloud deployment preferences
        \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Spring Framework Ecosystem Integration}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Spring Data JPA}: Automatic repository implementation and query generation (see \texttt{src/main/java/com/solar/*/repository/})
    \item \textbf{Spring Security}: JWT-based authentication implemented in \texttt{src/main/java/com/solar/user\_management/security/}
    \item \textbf{Spring Boot Actuator}: Production monitoring endpoints configured in \texttt{pom.xml} line 35
    \item \textbf{Spring WebSocket}: Real-time communication implemented in \texttt{src/main/java/com/solar/core\_services/energy\_monitoring/service/WebSocketService.java}
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Frontend Technology Decisions}

\textbf{Next.js 15.2.4 with React 19 and TypeScript}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Decision Rationale} (as specified in \texttt{solar\_frontend/package.json}):
        \begin{itemize}
            \item \textbf{Modern React Features}: React 19 with latest hooks and concurrent features
            \item \textbf{App Router}: File-based routing with layout support
            \item \textbf{TypeScript Integration}: Full type safety across components (see \texttt{solar\_frontend/tsconfig.json})
            \item \textbf{Performance}: Built-in optimization and code splitting
            \item \textbf{Real-time Communication}: Custom WebSocket hook implementation (see \texttt{solar\_frontend/hooks/useWebSocket.ts})
        \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{UI Framework Selection}:
        \begin{itemize}
            \item \textbf{Radix UI}: Accessible components (lines 13-40 in \texttt{solar\_frontend/package.json})
            \item \textbf{Tailwind CSS}: Utility-first styling configured in \texttt{solar\_frontend/tailwind.config.ts}
            \item \textbf{Recharts}: Data visualization for energy monitoring charts
            \item \textbf{React Hook Form}: Form validation and handling
            \item \textbf{Lucide React}: Icon library (line 49 in \texttt{solar\_frontend/package.json})
        \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Database Technology Decisions}

\textbf{H2 Database for Development and Testing}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Implementation} (as configured in \texttt{src/main/resources/application.properties}):
        \begin{itemize}
            \item \textbf{In-Memory Database}: Fast startup and testing (line 5: \texttt{jdbc:h2:mem:solardb})
            \item \textbf{Development Console}: H2 web console enabled for debugging (lines 15-16)
